course: dictionary
lesson: 9100
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. «Smack» can mean a hit with an open hand, a loud kiss, or exactly in the middle. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it. «The ball hit him smack on the nose.» The words «hit him» and «on the nose» tell you smack means exactly, right on.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense. «The ball hit him exactly on the nose» works, so the meaning is right. Smack can also be a verb, a noun or an adverb, so the job it does in the sentence is another clue.
explain: Smack can also mean to suggest something. «That smacks of cheating» means that suggests cheating. Here smack is not about hitting at all. Hitting is never a kind way to teach a person or an animal, and the example sentences show why: «fear and smacking make a dog anxious, not good.»
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Smack» as a verb means to hit someone hard with an open hand. Hitting is not OK.
fact: «Smack» as a noun means a hit with an open hand, or the loud sound of a hit.
fact: «Smack in the middle» means exactly in the middle, and it is an informal, everyday phrase.
fact: «Smack of» means to suggest something, as in «that smacks of cheating». Some meanings, like the illegal drug, are slang or old and are not for children to use.
exercise: «The ball hit him smack on the nose.» What does smack mean here? | To hit with an open hand, in anger | *Exactly, right on | To suggest something | A loud kiss
exercise: Maya says, «That smacks of cheating.» What does smacks of mean? | *To suggest something, here cheating | A loud kiss | Exactly in the middle | To hit someone hard
exercise: «Grandma gave me a loud smack on the cheek.» What does smack mean here? | A hit with a closed fist | *A loud kiss | Exactly in the middle | A small fishing boat
test: «Modern trainers use rewards, because fear and smacking make a dog anxious, not good.» Why do modern trainers avoid smacking? | It makes dogs too happy | It is a fun game for dogs | *It makes a dog anxious, and it is not a good way to train | It is the cheapest way to train
test: The bus stopped smack in the middle of the road. What does smack in the middle mean? | A loud bang | *Exactly in the middle | To hit with an open hand | Near the edge of the road
exam: Which meaning of smack is slang and not for children to use? | A loud kiss | Exactly in the middle | To suggest something | *An illegal drug
